    researchNote: 'Reframes as real, verifiable evaluation criteria (real $0-minimum/fractional-share data already verified for how-to-buy-stocks-online) rather than naming and rating specific unverified products.',
    citations: [],
    body: `<p>The criteria that matter for a beginner investing app differ meaningfully from what an experienced trader needs — simplicity and genuine cost transparency matter more than advanced tools.</p><h2>The Criteria to Evaluate</h2><p>Confirm <strong>$0 account minimums</strong> and <strong>fractional share support</strong> — standard among major platforms today, removing the barrier of needing a stock's full share price. Check for genuine educational content built into the platform, not just execution tools — a beginner benefits from accessible explanations alongside the ability to trade. Verify $0 commission on standard stock and ETF trades. And confirm the platform is a regulated broker with SIPC insurance protecting your account in the event of broker failure.</p><div class="callout callout-tip"><p><strong>A nuance worth flagging:</strong> A easy way to verify legitimate regulation: check the broker's registration directly on FINRA's BrokerCheck tool — a regulated platform will show up there with a verifiable registration history, a simple but often-skipped due-diligence step before depositing any funds.</p></div><div class="callout callout-info"><p><strong>Someone Choosing Their First Investing App:</strong> Verify FINRA registration via BrokerCheck before depositing funds.</p></div><div class="callout callout-info"><p><strong>Someone Wanting Built-In Learning Resources:</strong> Check for accessible educational content, not just execution tools.</p></div><h2>Evaluate Investing Apps the Way</h2><ol><li>Verify FINRA registration and SIPC coverage before funding an account.</li><li>Confirm $0 minimums and fractional share support.</li><li>Check for genuine educational content suited to your actual experience level.</li></ol><p>See <a href="/stocks/opening-a-brokerage-account">opening a brokerage account</a> for the fuller account-opening detail.</p>`,
