<p>The practical fix is treating any lump-sum disbursement (a loan refund, a semester's aid payment) as if it were a full semester's income, dividing it by the number of months it needs to cover before spending against it. Treating a large refund check as instantly spendable is one of the more common ways students end a semester short on money they thought they had.</p>
