<p>The secured-versus-unsecured line determines what a lender can actually do if payments stop — repossess a car, foreclose on a home — versus pursuing collections and credit damage without a specific asset to seize. It's also the main reason secured loans typically carry lower rates than unsecured ones: the lender's risk is genuinely lower with collateral backing the loan.</p>
