<p>What actually matters more than the starting amount is consistency. A modest, automated monthly contribution started now, given enough time for compound growth to work, can meaningfully outperform a larger one-time amount invested years later — because time in the market, not the size of any single contribution, is the dominant variable in long-term outcomes.</p>
